---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'

const images = [
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-116/01-the-sunbeam-funeral.png",
    "title": "The Sunbeam Funeral",
    "caption": "Epic wide shot: on a bleak, permanently gray alien wasteland, a druid stands with arms raised as a pillar of pure golden sunlight bursts upward from him and pierces the thick radiation clouds, the first sunlight this world has seen in ages. Around him a small funeral: a tiny Kobold paladin consecrating the ground, a Dragonborn fighter kneeling to place a dagger, a massive Goliath barbarian clashing metal in rhythm."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-116/02-sundr-declines-the-bugbear.png",
    "title": "Sundr Declines the Bugbear",
    "caption": "On scraggly, mutated grass beside a single withered flower of an unnatural color, a large furry bugbear body is forming from a single golden feather, its eyes still closed. Above it, the radiant ghostly spirit of an Aasimar sorcerer floats, relaxed and smiling, one hand raised in a polite \"no thanks\" wave, bathed in warm golden light from above."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-116/03-kiet-goes-brain-shopping.png",
    "title": "Kiet Goes Brain Shopping",
    "caption": "A comical, cartoonish scene in an alien mind flayer library: tall shelves lined with glowing glass jars, each holding a brain, some labeled, some lab-grown and eerily smooth. A Dragonborn fighter in studded leather pushes a small shopping basket down the aisle, squinting critically at a jar like he's picking produce at a supermarket."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-116/04-the-troll-funeral-pyre.png",
    "title": "The Troll Funeral Pyre",
    "caption": "Wide shot under a gray, storm-torn alien sky: a huge heap of hobbit-sized troll bodies, sloughed off from one giant mutant troll, burns on a funeral pyre. A Dragonborn fighter breathes a torrent of fire across it."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-116/05-haru-meets-qdv.png",
    "title": "Haru Meets QDV",
    "caption": "A cavernous mind flayer chamber with a giant, rotting elder brain slumped in a fetid green pool. A tiny Kobold paladin, gunked head to toe in slime with dried blood under his nose, is mid-air, flung back into the pool by a gangly mind flayer that has small daggers braided into its face tentacles."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-116/06-the-monument-tree.png",
    "title": "The Monument Tree",
    "caption": "Low angle looking up: a colossal petrified crystalline tree hundreds of feet tall on a dead gray world, its impossible branches held aloft against physics. Its leaves are tombstone-like crystal slabs carved with endless names, and its trunk is covered in script that fades into individual words higher up."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-116/07-the-uprising.png",
    "title": "The Uprising",
    "caption": "Freed slaves of a mind flayer lair revel in liberation: furry yeti-like quaggoths, mutant humans with noses growing all over their bodies, and stitched troll experiments kick and pile up the bodies of dead mind flayers, then dance around a roaring bonfire, singing with mouths open, a Les Misérables barricade energy. In the background, an adventuring party watches, and one lone living mind flayer looks on, dejected."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-116/08-if-you-would-dent-the-world.png",
    "title": "If You Would Dent the World",
    "caption": "In a ruined, irradiated village, mutant seers with translucent skin and fish-like mouths, and a figure wearing robes made entirely of writhing worms, lead an adventuring party into a crumbling storehouse stacked floor to ceiling with ancient crates of mining explosives and bundled dynamite. The Dragonborn fighter grins wide."
  }
]
---

<Layout title="Session 116 — Tales of the Radiant Citadel" description="The party buried their dead. They burned the honorable troll on a pyre, and Toven reincarnated Sundr into a bugbear body. Sundr's spirit politely declined ">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <a href="/studio" class="text-sm text-earth hover:text-ink transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">&larr; Studio</a>

    <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black leading-tight mb-2">
      Session 116
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-earth mb-1">Tales of the Radiant Citadel &middot; October 6, 2026</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-light mb-8">Bluetspur Expedition (Aftermath)</p>

    <div class="prose-section text-ink-light leading-relaxed mb-12 space-y-4">
      <p>
        The party buried their dead. They burned the honorable troll on a pyre, and Toven reincarnated Sundr into a bugbear body. Sundr's spirit politely declined to stay: he's in the Sunweaver's country club now, playing golf with the big guy. His funeral brought the first sunlight Bluetspur had seen in ages. Haru woke in the God Brain's rotting pool and met Kualdau Vaux (QDV), the last mind flayer of the God Brain's network, played by Erik as a temp character. QDV guided the party through the lair and to the Monument Tree. There the tree revealed the possible futures, the Lady in the Black Veil's true name (Kyosal Inja), and the High Master's weakness. A village of mutant resistance descendants then offered the one resource they have: piles of explosives.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Highlights</h2>
    <ul class="text-sm text-ink-light leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-12 list-disc list-inside">
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Troll Funeral Pyre</strong> — The storm killed the mutant troll, and it sloughed apart into a pile of &quot;mini trolls.&quot; Sam: *&quot;When I say mini trolls, I mean compared to the huge guys. So mini trolls are still like hobbit-sized.&quot;* Table: *&quot;I was hoping for like toy-sized.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Haru Wakes in the Pool; Enter QDV</strong> — Haru rolls a 1 on the d4, so he wakes after one hour at 1 HP and uses Lay on Hands on himself for 20.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">&quot;We Did Not Start This Thing&quot;</strong> — Haru reunites with the party: *&quot;Good news and bad news. Good news is lots of Mind Flayers are dead, nearly all of them as it turns out. Bad news, Sundr did die to make this happen... Medium news, this dude grabbed me and threw me around, but I think he's trying to be friendly.&quot;* / QDV: *&quot;You attacked me!&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Kiet Goes Brain Shopping</strong> — No coins or treasure: *&quot;The mind flayers don't seem to use that sort of an economy.&quot;* There is plenty of strange lab gear, though, possibly of interest to Sigmar back at the bastion.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Uprising</strong> — The freed quaggoths, mutants, and troll experiments ask: *&quot;Are you the masters now?&quot;* / *&quot;No, you are your own masters now... There was a dream that was Rome.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Reincarnate: Sundr Declines the Bugbear</strong> — The party debated using Sundr's toes and feather. One argument: *&quot;There was a sense of completion to the way that he went out.&quot;* Then the metagame: &quot;I'm like 90% certain that if Erik wanted his character to come back, he wouldn't send us an intro video to his next character... I'm holding up my metagaming fingers.&quot;</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Sundr's Funeral</strong> — Toven casts Sunbeam straight up as a pillar: *&quot;I am embracing the sun as Sundr would have.&quot;* Sam: &quot;This is perhaps the first time there has been a beam of pure sunlight here in Bluetspur for a very long time.&quot; Also: *&quot;There are no vampires presently in the party to immediately be fried by this.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">QDV, Lord of the Cranium Rats</strong> — Twelve: *&quot;Our agreement has come to culmination... And our people will be reconnected with the mind flayers of this world... once again, we will have purpose.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Monument Tree</strong> — Sam: *&quot;This tree is hundreds of feet tall. Its branches are being held aloft through an impossibility of physics... As you go higher, it seems more like just words, endless individual words up and down the length of the tree.&quot;* Its leaves are tombstone-like crystal slabs covered in names.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Kyosal Inja — The Lady in the Black Veil</strong> — QDV: *&quot;Strangely, my intelligence is not as high as my charisma.&quot;* / &quot;That's because you're dumb.&quot;</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The High Master's Weakness</strong> — The High Master is an Elder Brain grafted onto a dragon. It has Legendary Resistance and a breath of tadpole brine. Its tentacle grab stops spellcasting and breaks concentration. It is immune to psychic damage.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Mutant Village: Explosives</strong> — Sam: *&quot;Translucent skin, fish-flabby-mouthed seers. Beings in robes made entirely of worms.&quot;*</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Art</h2>
    <div class="space-y-10">
      {images.map((img) => (
        <figure>
          <img
            src={img.src}
            alt={img.title}
            class="w-full rounded-xl shadow-lg"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-3">
            <span class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm">{img.title}</span>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-light mt-1">{img.caption}</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="border-t border-cream-dark mt-16 pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold mb-3">Party</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Sundr / QDV (temp)</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Erik)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Kiet</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Jonas)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Virgil Gemnar</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Kyle)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Toven</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Max)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Haru</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Hunter)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">DM</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Sam)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
